{"id": "EUVD-2026-45621", "enisaUuid": "6cf3614b-8546-3805-925f-331e1e8f337c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: reject CHID-0 ACCEPT that matches an empty ism_dev slot\n\nOn the SMC-D client, slot 0 of ini->ism_dev[]/ini->ism_chid[] is\nreserved for an SMC-Dv1 device. smc_find_ism_v2_device_clnt()\npopulates V2 entries starting at index 1, so when no V1 device is\nselected slot 0 is left in its kzalloc()'ed state with ism_dev[0] ==\nNULL and ism_chid[0] == 0.\n\nsmc_v2_determine_accepted_chid() then matches the peer's CHID against\nthe array starting from index 0 using the CHID alone. A malicious\npeer replying to a SMC-Dv2-only proposal with d1.chid == 0 matches\nthe empty slot, ini->ism_selected becomes 0, and the subsequent\nism_dev[0]->lgr_lock dereference in smc_conn_create() faults at\noffsetof(struct smcd_dev, lgr_lock) == 0x68:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: null-ptr-deref in _raw_spin_lock_bh+0x79/0xe0\n  Write of size 4 at addr 0000000000000068 by task exploit/144\n  Call Trace:\n   _raw_spin_lock_bh\n   smc_conn_create (net/smc/smc_core.c:1997)\n   __smc_connect (net/smc/af_smc.c:1447)\n   smc_connect (net/smc/af_smc.c:1720)\n   __sys_connect\n   __x64_sys_connect\n   do_syscall_64\n\nRequire ism_dev[i] to be non-NULL before accepting a CHID match.", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T15:39:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:28:10", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/903f7688ffeb9b323d70652c01f554bd4ba2a3d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd2f9dd83c68abd7ba7ded7075290b016cb7ecd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6927cacf2b10d4fa80c1a2d407512ef9397c59c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d38ba387244e5c5f7db3e11ea98bc2c7beccb0c0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/53eb7bd09aace72fa17510d80e0caf5ca058c231", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/afa9036b8c9963947b487c36e332df6a42c96fcb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65edb3b0822cfe5041be8fbabebd57e2e5ad9f4e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/277740023def559a4a2ddc3e8e784ee37a0f16a9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64048", "GHSA-942p-vjp4-xm8p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05ab4584-6b2a-3f8e-8eda-1c9fd9edd90d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7c9c5f4af7f6098da68705fc5d86565d0728ef7 <903f7688ffeb9b323d70652c01f554bd4ba2a3d6"}, {"id": "0c187db1-1fb7-3481-8554-c884a6411aa8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.175"}, {"id": "1121eb44-a58c-3315-abc2-2e0c8b5f8c1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7c9c5f4af7f6098da68705fc5d86565d0728ef7 <65edb3b0822cfe5041be8fbabebd57e2e5ad9f4e"}, {"id": "1345f0c1-5a13-3c53-949f-8a11d7ce4c3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7c9c5f4af7f6098da68705fc5d86565d0728ef7 <d38ba387244e5c5f7db3e11ea98bc2c7beccb0c0"}, {"id": "1aa4c2ac-6a18-3415-929f-470c4c0cbe51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7c9c5f4af7f6098da68705fc5d86565d0728ef7 <dd2f9dd83c68abd7ba7ded7075290b016cb7ecd0"}, {"id": "2fc44efb-3eba-3803-a1a7-957a6f341cd9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.217"}, {"id": "366487dc-002d-3fdb-8b63-82f80ce8c07c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.92"}, {"id": "383bab27-9906-3861-8728-890395c8936a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.34"}, {"id": "45893cf5-37a0-349f-af88-98422d9eea6a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.11"}, {"id": "4ccc8950-a1e6-3f05-88e5-906cdfc4220a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.142"}, {"id": "5b66d61d-810c-3e10-951b-0297